1
00:00:02,330 --> 00:00:05,190
我们都漂浮在时间的河流里
We all float along the river of time.

2
00:00:06,150 --> 00:00:08,240
但是这条河有没有起源？
But does that river have a source?

3
00:00:09,590 --> 00:00:11,500
时间是怎么开始的？
How was time unleashed?

4
00:00:13,020 --> 00:00:16,450
有人认为时间会永远而平顺地流动
Some believe time flows smoothly and eternally.

5
00:00:17,150 --> 00:00:19,540
有人认为时间根本不会流动
Others say it doesn't flow at all --

6
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:23,550
而是在每一个刹那间诞生
it pops into existence every fraction of a second.

7
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:29,010
物理学专家对此各有看法
The finest minds in physics can't agree.

8
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:32,060
然而新的实验或许可以回答
But new experiments may hold the answer

9
00:00:32,060 --> 00:00:37,520
宇宙史上最玄的未解之谜
to the greatest unsolved mystery in the history of the universe.

10
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:39,620
也就是
The mystery...

11
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:42,210
时间的起点
Of when time began.

12
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:52,090
空间，时间，生命本身。
Space, time, life itself.

13
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:57,750
宇宙的奥秘，尽在穿越虫洞。
The secrets of the cosmos lie through the wormhole.

14
00:01:05,170 --> 00:01:08,890
时间何时开始？

15
00:01:12,730 --> 00:01:13,670
你是何时出生的？
When were you born?

16
00:01:15,020 --> 00:01:17,120
这个问题看似简单
Sounds like a simple question.

17
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:19,400
答案就是某年某月某日
You just say a certain year, a month, and day.

18
00:01:20,180 --> 00:01:22,460
但是世界各地的人对时间的概念并不同
But around the world, we reckon time differently.

19
00:01:23,910 --> 00:01:26,770
根据沙乌地阿拉伯所用历法现在是15世纪
In Saudi Arabia, it's the 15th century.

20
00:01:26,780 --> 00:01:28,870
根据以色列所用历法现在是58世纪
In Israel, it's the 58th.

21
00:01:29,850 --> 00:01:32,520
我们生活在24个不同的时区
And we live in 24 different time zones.

22
00:01:33,380 --> 00:01:36,610
我们在测量时间时，都会有个起点
We all measure time relative to some starting point --

23
00:01:37,310 --> 00:01:38,650
这是我们选择的点
a point we have chosen.

24
00:01:39,410 --> 00:01:42,470
但如果我们要了解时间的本质
But if we really want to know what time it is,

25
00:01:42,660 --> 00:01:45,710
就得知道宇宙的钟是从何时开始走的
we need to know when the cosmic clock started to tick.

26
00:01:47,050 --> 00:01:49,530
时间是否跟宇宙一同开始？
Did time begin when the universe began?

27
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:52,770
还是以别的方式开始？
Or did it start some other way?

28
00:01:58,370 --> 00:02:00,090
我曾经跟人比赛骑单车
Once, I was in a bike race.

29
00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:04,470
我想让朋友见识我的超快速度
I wanted to impress some friends with my terrific speed.

30
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:09,250
所以我卯足全力
So I gave it everything I had.

31
00:02:11,160 --> 00:02:12,680
比赛结果很接近
It was a close race --

32
00:02:12,690 --> 00:02:15,360
真的很接近 我还以为是平手
so close, I thought it was a tie.

33
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:19,390
其中一人说我的对手比较快
One kid said my opponent was quickest.

34
00:02:20,370 --> 00:02:22,090
但是另一人说我比较快
But another said I was faster.

35
00:02:23,430 --> 00:02:26,100
谁对时间的观念才是对的？
So, whose perception of time was correct?

36
00:02:27,250 --> 00:02:29,530
就某种意义上我们都是对的
In a way, we were all right.

37
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:36,400
时间是测量变化的量度
Time is a measure of change.

38
00:02:39,090 --> 00:02:41,200
但我们怎么知道事物有改变？
But how do we know things change?

39
00:02:42,550 --> 00:02:44,830
我们会依靠我们的感官传送资讯
We rely on what our senses tell us,

40
00:02:45,030 --> 00:02:48,380
其中最主要的就是视觉
and primarily, we rely on what we can see.

41
00:02:48,660 --> 00:02:50,570
所以我们会依靠光
We rely on light.

42
00:02:51,720 --> 00:02:53,440
在真空里
In the vacuum of space,

43
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:58,210
光速恒为每秒18万6千里
light travels at a fixed speed of 186,000 miles per second.

44
00:03:01,510 --> 00:03:04,940
这是大家公认的宇宙真理
This is accepted as an absolute truth of the universe.

45
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:09,330
宇宙学家珍娜莱文说 如此一来
And that, says cosmologist Janna Levin,

46
00:03:09,830 --> 00:03:12,890
光和时间就有了独特的关系
gives light a unique relationship to time.

47
00:03:14,030 --> 00:03:15,880
光速是固定的
It's actually completely remarkable

48
00:03:15,880 --> 00:03:17,470
这真的很神奇
that the speed of light is an absolute.

49
00:03:17,660 --> 00:03:20,330
它不会变快 也不会变慢
It's never faster. It's never slower.

50
00:03:20,340 --> 00:03:22,430
为了了解时间的相对性
To understand the relativity of time,

51
00:03:22,630 --> 00:03:24,340
我们必须了解光
we really need to understand light,

52
00:03:24,340 --> 00:03:26,620
一旦我们开始思考光的本质
and once we start thinking about the nature of light,

53
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:30,270
我们熟悉的观念将会彻底改变
all of our familiar intuitions are turned on their heads.

54
00:03:31,330 --> 00:03:33,420
如果光速是固定的
If the speed of light is constant,

55
00:03:33,620 --> 00:03:37,230
那时间和空间之所以出现变化和扭曲
then time and space must shift and distort

56
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:40,290
就是因为个人的观点不同
depending on your particular point of view.

57
00:03:42,430 --> 00:03:45,280
爱因斯坦洞察到一个非常深奥的理论
Einstein had this very profound insight

58
00:03:45,480 --> 00:03:48,540
是在探索像光这种简单事物时想透的
when he started to think about something as simple as light,

59
00:03:49,430 --> 00:03:51,910
他发现到...
and he realized that

60
00:03:52,100 --> 00:03:53,430
如果对于宇宙的
if light was going to be the same

61
00:03:53,430 --> 00:03:55,340
每个人而言光都是一样的
for everybody in the universe

62
00:03:55,540 --> 00:03:57,000
他们的移动速度
regardless of how fast they were moving

63
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,970
跟所在位置都没有影响
or where they were in the universe,

64
00:03:58,980 --> 00:04:01,530
那么每个观测者所谓的
then space and time had to be different

65
00:04:01,540 --> 00:04:03,410
时间和空间就不会一样
for different observers.

66
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:06,550
也就是说时间是很个人的
This means time is very personal.

67
00:04:06,730 --> 00:04:10,540
你的位置跟速度会决定时间
It depends on where you are and how fast you are moving.

68
00:04:10,740 --> 00:04:13,600
你认为自己的行动多快多慢
And the way you see your movement through time

69
00:04:13,610 --> 00:04:17,040
可能跟别人所认为的不一样
may not be the way others see your movement through time.

70
00:04:23,580 --> 00:04:26,440
比方说 珍娜有个分身
Say, for instance, Janna has a doppelganger

71
00:04:26,440 --> 00:04:29,500
这个分身在纽约搭地铁跟计程车
that rides the subways and taxis of New York.

72
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:34,070
如果珍娜的分身坐上计程车
If Janna's doppelganger gets in a cab

73
00:04:34,270 --> 00:04:37,130
而计程车的速度快得不可思议
and that cab travels at incredible speeds...

74
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:43,080
珍娜跟分身时间流逝的速度就会不同
...time will flow differently for each woman.

75
00:04:44,510 --> 00:04:46,110
如果她坐计程车跟我擦身而过
If she flies past me in a taxi,

76
00:04:46,310 --> 00:04:49,360
在我眼里她的时间流逝得比较慢
it will appear to me that her time is running slower.

77
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:54,030
在我分身的眼里，我跟身处的这条街道
From my doppelganger's point of view, the street with me on it,

78
00:04:54,230 --> 00:04:56,560
是以反方向跟她擦身而过的
we're flying past her in the opposite direction,

79
00:04:56,660 --> 00:04:59,340
她会觉得她的时间很正常
and as far as she's concerned, her time is normal.

80
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:01,530
反而是我的时间流逝得比较慢
It's my time that's running slow.

81
00:05:04,140 --> 00:05:06,810
为了了解这种现象
To understand why this happens,

82
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:10,620
请想像珍娜启动了双头雷射
imagine Janna turns on a double-sided laser

83
00:05:10,630 --> 00:05:14,510
脉冲光束打到骑楼的
whose pulsing beams bounce off the sidewalk below her

84
00:05:14,510 --> 00:05:17,670
地板跟天花板时就会反弹
and the balcony above her head.

85
00:05:17,840 --> 00:05:20,120
这个脉冲形成了光的时钟
The pulses form a light clock.

86
00:05:20,130 --> 00:05:23,560
每弹回一次就是一次滴答
Each bounce of the laser beam is one tick.

87
00:05:23,760 --> 00:05:26,430
珍娜眼中的光束是上下移动的
Janna sees the light go straight up and down,

88
00:05:26,430 --> 00:05:30,620
但是计程车里的分身会看到不同的景象
but her cab-riding double sees something quite different.

89
00:05:31,590 --> 00:05:33,870
从计程车的角度来看
From the perspective of the cab,

90
00:05:33,880 --> 00:05:37,110
光似乎变成了长长的斜线
the light appears to take a long diagonal

91
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:41,510
所以我的时钟似乎跑得很慢
and so seems as though my clock is taking too long to tick.

92
00:05:41,520 --> 00:05:44,590
因此我的时间看起来流逝得很慢
So it seems like my time is running slow.

93
00:05:45,460 --> 00:05:48,280
如果珍娜的分身在计程车里打开雷射
If Janna's doppelganger turns on the laser in the taxi,

94
00:05:49,190 --> 00:05:51,510
她眼中的光束也会垂直打到计程车的
she will see the beam hitting the ceiling and floor

95
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:53,560
车顶跟地板
right above and below her.

96
00:05:54,540 --> 00:05:59,510
但是街上的珍娜会认为这个光是沿着斜线移动的
But the Janna on the street sees the beam move diagonally.

97
00:05:59,510 --> 00:06:04,080
因为光束移动的距离变长时间看起来就变慢
Because the beam has longer to travel, its tick looks slower.

98
00:06:04,660 --> 00:06:08,520
如果我从街上往计程车里看
From my perspective on the street, if I'm looking into the taxi,

99
00:06:08,520 --> 00:06:10,990
我会看到她的光是长长的斜线
I see their light take a long diagonal,

100
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:14,430
我会觉得她的滴答声很长
and so I think it's taking their clock too long to tick.

101
00:06:14,630 --> 00:06:17,100
从我的观点来看，她的时钟很慢
From my perspective, their clocks are running slow.

102
00:06:20,660 --> 00:06:22,940
速度愈快 这种效应就愈明显
The effect increases the faster you go.

103
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:25,720
如果计程车的速度接近光速
If the cab approaches the speed of light,

104
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:27,720
也就是宇宙的速度极限
the speed limit of the universe,

105
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:32,110
计程车外头的时间看起来会是静止的
time outside the cab appears to stand still.

106
00:06:33,490 --> 00:06:36,730
如果那辆计程车以光速经过
If that taxi was to fly by at the speed of light,

107
00:06:36,740 --> 00:06:39,220
我的时钟看起来就会像停住一样
it would look like my clock was never going to tick,

108
00:06:39,220 --> 00:06:42,650
我的时间静止 就好像是冻结了
like my time had stood still, like time was frozen.

109
00:06:43,610 --> 00:06:45,510
那么哪个观测者才是对的？
So, which observer is correct?

110
00:06:46,100 --> 00:06:48,570
是站着不动的珍娜？
The Janna who's standing still?

111
00:06:48,580 --> 00:06:50,100
是车里的分身？
Or the Janna in motion?

112
00:06:52,250 --> 00:06:54,570
我跟分身对于时间的流动会有
My doppelganger and I just fundamentally disagree

113
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:55,870
截然不同的认识
on the passage of time,

114
00:06:55,870 --> 00:06:56,680
然而我们都是对的
and it's true. We're both right --

115
00:06:57,590 --> 00:06:58,920
时间是相对的
time is relative.

116
00:07:00,830 --> 00:07:04,840
相对性就表示没有单一的世界时
Relativity means that there can be no single universal time.

117
00:07:05,420 --> 00:07:07,510
然而过去曾有那么一刻
However, there was one moment

118
00:07:07,710 --> 00:07:10,760
所有的时间观点都一定是相同的
when all perspectives on time must have been the same --

119
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:15,910
那时候一切都存在于单一的点
a moment when everything existed in one single place...

120
00:07:16,110 --> 00:07:17,550
那一刻就是大爆作
The big bang.

121
00:07:18,710 --> 00:07:22,500
大爆炸跟宇宙诞生的理论
One of the hardest things to grasp about the idea of the

122
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:24,540
最叫人难以理解的
big bang and the creation of the universe

123
00:07:25,540 --> 00:07:30,580
就是想到时间可能源自于这个重大事件
is the idea that time itself may have begun in that big event,

124
00:07:30,780 --> 00:07:33,440
大爆炸创造了空间
that space was created in the big bang

125
00:07:33,440 --> 00:07:35,510
也让时间开始流动
and time began to tick.

126
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:40,510
在大爆炸之前时间或空间可能都不存在
Before our big bang, there might not have been space or time.

127
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:44,280
珍娜认为大爆作
Janna believes the big bang was probably

128
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:48,470
可能是宇宙中所有时间之流的源头
when all the various time streams in the universe began

129
00:07:48,550 --> 00:07:49,570
从那一刻起
and that, since then,

130
00:07:49,570 --> 00:07:53,200
不同地方的移动速度不同
time has passed differently in different places

131
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:56,500
各地时间就会出现差异
depending on how those places have moved.

132
00:07:56,560 --> 00:08:00,230
但是我们能否在宇宙中创造一些地方
But could we create places in our universe where

133
00:08:00,230 --> 00:08:04,040
让时间暂停，再重新开始？
time can appear to stop and then begin again?

134
00:08:06,150 --> 00:08:08,430
如果我们能让某个事件躲过光
If we could hide an event from light,

135
00:08:09,010 --> 00:08:10,910
我们能不能也让它躲过时间？
could we also hide it from time?

136
00:08:14,560 --> 00:08:19,750
艾力克斯加艾塔教授正在探索这些问题
These are questions Professor Alex Gaeta asked himself.

137
00:08:19,750 --> 00:08:21,650
艾力克斯曾是网球比赛选手
A former competition-tennis player,

138
00:08:21,660 --> 00:08:25,520
如今则是康乃尔大学的物理学家
Alex is a physicist at Cornell university

139
00:08:25,720 --> 00:08:28,390
他专门研究超快光学
specializing in ultra-fast optics.

140
00:08:30,210 --> 00:08:34,600
这项科技通常是用来高速传输数据的
This technology is usually used for high-speed data transmission.

141
00:08:34,980 --> 00:08:39,650
但是看过帝国学院的理论学家所写的一篇论文后
But after reading a paper written by theorists at imperial college,

142
00:08:39,660 --> 00:08:43,600
让他发现这项科技也能制造时间缺口
he realized it could also create a gap in time.

143
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:46,840
光是一种电磁扰动
You know, light is an electromagnetic disturbance.

144
00:08:46,850 --> 00:08:50,280
事物一旦出现变化就表示时间正在流动
The minute things start that's an indication changing, that time is passing.

145
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:52,160
这些变化会
So all these changes are

146
00:08:52,160 --> 00:08:54,860
产生很多电磁扰动
creating all these that are occurring electromagnetic disturbances

147
00:08:55,060 --> 00:08:59,550
只要侦测跟度量这些扰动就能得知时间的流动
that we can detect and measure as passage of time.

148
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:01,270
我们想出一种方法
What we've figured out is a way

149
00:09:01,470 --> 00:09:03,800
就是把光关掉
of essentially turning off the lights,

150
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:06,570
再把它打开
turning them back on without,

151
00:09:06,670 --> 00:09:11,060
但是你不会察觉到光有被关掉
you know, you sensing that they've ever actually been turned off.

152
00:09:15,640 --> 00:09:19,070
想像你可以把形成时间的光关掉很久
What would happen if you turned off the light shining on time

153
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:21,360
久到能够隐藏一个事件
long enough to hide an event?

154
00:09:22,820 --> 00:09:27,010
比方说 艾力克斯跟儿子马克思的比数相近
Say, for instance, Alex is in a close game with his son, Max.

155
00:09:27,590 --> 00:09:31,020
他就要拿到局点，而他很想赢
He's coming up to match point, and he wants to win.

156
00:09:31,790 --> 00:09:34,460
如果艾力克斯可以制造时间缺口
If Alex could create a hole in time,

157
00:09:35,420 --> 00:09:37,700
就不会有人看到他做这件事
no one could see him do this...

158
00:09:41,530 --> 00:09:44,510
对于观测者而言，包括他儿子在内
To observers, including his son,

159
00:09:45,390 --> 00:09:47,490
艾力克斯赢得这一盘，中间毫无暂停
Alex wins the set without pause.

160
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:53,590
目前这还是不可能的事
Right now, this is impossible.

161
00:09:53,790 --> 00:09:56,270
然而聚沙可以成塔
But all great things start small.

162
00:10:02,420 --> 00:10:04,900
这是艾力克斯相当重要的实验仪器
This is the key component of Alex's experiment --

163
00:10:05,670 --> 00:10:07,190
叫做分时透镜
the split-time lens.

164
00:10:08,340 --> 00:10:10,620
它可以聚焦时间的光信号
It focuses light signals and time

165
00:10:10,820 --> 00:10:13,490
就像玻璃透镜可以聚焦空间的光
the way a glass lens focuses light in space.

166
00:10:14,450 --> 00:10:17,880
在真空中，光速是固定的
In a vacuum, the speed of light is constant,

167
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:22,500
但是它的速度可能会改变
but that speed changes when light passes through a material

168
00:10:22,500 --> 00:10:25,580
可能因为光穿过物体或是碰到其他光束
or when it runs into another light beam.

169
00:10:26,350 --> 00:10:30,360
艾力克斯的分时透镜同时运用这两种诀窍
Alex's split-time lens uses both tricks.

170
00:10:32,090 --> 00:10:34,940
艾力克斯先把雷射打进光束
Alex shoots a laser into a beam of light,

171
00:10:34,950 --> 00:10:36,850
让光速稍微变慢
slowing it ever so slightly.

172
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:42,390
接着光束穿过玻璃纤维，一分为二
The beam then passes through a glass fiber where it splits into two parts,

173
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:44,620
这两道光的波长不同
each with a different wavelength.

174
00:10:44,630 --> 00:10:48,060
波长较短的光行进速度比较快
The lower wavelength pulls ahead of the higher wavelength,

175
00:10:48,260 --> 00:10:50,930
因此能制造出完全黑暗的缺口
leaving a gap of absolute darkness.

176
00:10:51,310 --> 00:10:54,550
在这个缺口的东西无法被观测到
Anything within that gap is impossible to observe

177
00:10:54,560 --> 00:10:56,270
因为这里没有光
since there is no light there.

178
00:10:57,230 --> 00:11:01,420
接着两道光通过另一个分时透镜并合而为一
The light then passes through another time lens that re-unifies

179
00:11:01,430 --> 00:11:04,150
因而看不出任何变化
the beam with no visible change.

180
00:11:09,310 --> 00:11:13,360
艾力克斯曾用这个装置制造出缺口
Using this device, Alex has created gaps

181
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:15,840
将近10亿分之1秒的时间缺口
that last almost a billionth of a second.

182
00:11:16,580 --> 00:11:18,290
听起来似乎很小
That may not sound like much,

183
00:11:18,490 --> 00:11:21,570
但是在高速传输资讯的世界里
but in the world of high-speed information transfer,

184
00:11:21,570 --> 00:11:22,910
这段时间相当长
it's significant.

185
00:11:23,670 --> 00:11:25,010
比方说，你有一串数据流
Let's say you have a data stream

186
00:11:25,010 --> 00:11:26,910
而你不想要打断它
and you don't want to interrupt it at all

187
00:11:27,110 --> 00:11:30,550
但是你想把某个资讯放进数据流
but you want to put some information into that data stream

188
00:11:30,560 --> 00:11:31,790
再把它拿出来
and then take it out.

189
00:11:32,690 --> 00:11:34,210
只要这样制造缺口
So, by creating this gap,

190
00:11:34,220 --> 00:11:36,890
你不用打断数据流也能制造缺口
you can create the gap, not disturb the light stream,

191
00:11:37,080 --> 00:11:39,940
从而插入一点资讯传输出去
insert a little bit of data, transmit it,

192
00:11:39,940 --> 00:11:41,850
稍后再取出来
and then later on, pull out that data

193
00:11:42,620 --> 00:11:44,520
最后让资讯流合而为一
and then put the data stream back together.

194
00:11:45,480 --> 00:11:48,720
这个资讯就会从时间里消失
And that information would be hidden from the passage of time.

195
00:11:53,350 --> 00:11:57,740
现在如果要制造1秒的时间缺口
Today, creating a light gap that lasts for one second

196
00:11:57,740 --> 00:12:01,750
需要18万6千里长的机器
would require a machine 186,000 miles long.

197
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:06,330
因此艾力克斯得凭真本事才能打赢这一场
So Alex will have to win his tennis matches the hard way.

198
00:12:07,100 --> 00:12:10,330
但是科技进化的速度极快
But the technology is rapidly evolving.

199
00:12:11,320 --> 00:12:13,220
原则上在某些实验里
In principle, there have been demonstrations

200
00:12:13,420 --> 00:12:17,230
你可以让光速减慢一千万到一亿倍
where they can slow down light by factors of 10 to the 7th, 10 to the 8th.

201
00:12:17,430 --> 00:12:19,710
再过不久 或许可以减得更慢
In the near future, it could be even more.

202
00:12:19,720 --> 00:12:21,440
你几乎可以让光停下来
You could essentially almost stop light,

203
00:12:21,630 --> 00:12:25,330
并且相对来说 长时间把光储存起来 比如几秒
store light for relatively long periods of time, seconds,

204
00:12:25,580 --> 00:12:27,480
再把光释放出去
and then essentially release it to travel,

205
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:30,160
让它回到原本的光速
again, back at the speed of light.

206
00:12:31,690 --> 00:12:32,830
艾力克斯跟珍娜的研究
Alex and Janna's work

207
00:12:33,030 --> 00:12:38,550
探讨了观测者，光以及时间流动的深切关联
explores the deep connection between observers, light, and the passage of time.

208
00:12:39,140 --> 00:12:40,470
这让我们不禁纳闷
It begs the question,

209
00:12:40,850 --> 00:12:44,590
要是没人看到 时间还会存在吗？
does time exist if there is no one around to see it?

210
00:12:45,650 --> 00:12:47,360
这位科学家认为答案是否定的
One scientist says no --

211
00:12:48,510 --> 00:12:51,750
时间的起点比我们想的要晚得多
time began much later than we think.

212
00:12:59,570 --> 00:13:02,420
你有多少次在漆黑的房间醒来
How often have you woken up in a darkened room

213
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:05,480
却不晓得当时是几点？
and had no idea what time it was?

214
00:13:06,450 --> 00:13:10,640
你睡了几分钟？还是几小时？
Have you been out for minutes or hours?

215
00:13:11,990 --> 00:13:16,180
你在睡觉时感觉不到时间经过
When you are sleeping, you have no sense that time is passing.

216
00:13:16,950 --> 00:13:20,500
也许宇宙对时间的感觉也是一样
Perhaps the cosmos experiences time in the same way.

217
00:13:20,960 --> 00:13:24,820
大爆炸是宇宙诞生的时刻
The big bang was the moment our universe was born,

218
00:13:25,010 --> 00:13:28,630
但要是宇宙没有马上醒来呢？
but what if it didn't wake up right away?

219
00:13:29,980 --> 00:13:33,990
宇宙是否曾经有段时间是没有时间的？
Could there have been a time when the universe had no time?

220
00:13:40,590 --> 00:13:44,040
赖瑞舒曼教授在德国的德勒斯登感觉有点格格不入
Professor Larry Schulman is a little out of place in dresden, Germany.

221
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:47,570
他来自纽约的克拉克森大学
His home base is New York's Clarkson university,

222
00:13:47,570 --> 00:13:50,240
那里时常笼罩在静止的积雪里
which often sits under a static sheet of ice.

223
00:13:51,770 --> 00:13:55,510
赖瑞说那就跟早期的宇宙没什么两样
Not so different, Larry says, from the state of the early universe,

224
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:59,320
他说在那时候时间并不存在
when, he claims, time did not exist.

225
00:14:03,270 --> 00:14:08,240
赖瑞研究大量粒子形成的系统行为
Larry explores the behavior of systems composed of large numbers of particles

226
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:11,290
像是这座喷泉的水 或是宇宙
such as the water in this fountain or the universe.

227
00:14:12,060 --> 00:14:14,340
统计力学也可以告诉我们
Statistical mechanics can also tell us

228
00:14:14,540 --> 00:14:17,010
光和时间的关系
about the relationship of light to time.

229
00:14:18,160 --> 00:14:21,440
光携带事件的资讯
Light carries information about events.

230
00:14:21,530 --> 00:14:25,500
我们用光来断定现在的情况
We use it to determine what is happening now.

231
00:14:25,550 --> 00:14:27,640
但是因为光速有极限
But because light has a speed limit,

232
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:32,650
所以我们看到的其实都是过去的事件
everything we see actually took place in the past.

233
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:37,510
比方说 阳光照到地球要8分钟左右
The time it would take, for example, from the Sun is about 8 minutes

234
00:14:37,510 --> 00:14:39,030
因为相隔9300万里
because it's 93 million miles,

235
00:14:39,230 --> 00:14:42,660
除以光速每秒18万6千里
and you figure with a velocity of 186,000 miles per second,

236
00:14:42,860 --> 00:14:44,380
差不多要这么久的时间
that's how long the light would take.

237
00:14:44,390 --> 00:14:47,860
比方说 要是太阳爆炸了
So, if the Sun were to explode, for example,

238
00:14:47,860 --> 00:14:51,290
你要到8分钟以后才会知道
you would not know about it until eight minutes after the event.

239
00:14:53,500 --> 00:14:55,400
我们所见宇宙最遥远的光
The light of the most distant parts of the universe

240
00:14:55,410 --> 00:14:59,600
来自138亿光年之外的地方
has been traveling toward us for 13.8 billion years.

241
00:14:59,990 --> 00:15:04,600
这就是大爆炸初创宇宙的时刻
This is when the universe began in the big bang.

242
00:15:09,010 --> 00:15:12,820
早期的宇宙只是带电的粒子场
The early universe was nothing but a field of charged particles,

243
00:15:12,830 --> 00:15:15,110
是高温高密度的电浆云
a dense, hot cloud of plasma.

244
00:15:15,880 --> 00:15:21,510
光子在这团电浆云里跑不远
Photons, particles of light, could not travel very far in this soup.

245
00:15:22,560 --> 00:15:27,570
宇宙形成38万年左右之后
Then about 380,000 years into the life of the universe,

246
00:15:27,570 --> 00:15:30,630
突然出现一种变化 叫做重组
there was a sudden change called recombination.

247
00:15:31,970 --> 00:15:34,250
这时原子开始形成
This is when atoms began to form.

248
00:15:35,210 --> 00:15:36,340
在重组之前
Prior to recombination,

249
00:15:36,340 --> 00:15:38,160
如果电子跟质子
if an electron and a proton

250
00:15:38,160 --> 00:15:39,980
靠近并短暂结合
would approach and bind temporarily,

251
00:15:40,180 --> 00:15:43,990
就会被另一个冲过来的光子打散
they would be whacked by a photon coming along and be knocked apart.

252
00:15:44,590 --> 00:15:46,870
有了重组这个过程
Recombination is a process

253
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:50,620
先前散布在电浆里的
in which the electrons and the protons, which were previously

254
00:15:50,620 --> 00:15:52,600
电子和质子
loose and separated from each other in the plasma,

255
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:54,320
终于能够结合起来
finally can get together.

256
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:00,640
这跟曲棍球有点像
It's a bit like hockey.

257
00:16:01,510 --> 00:16:04,370
光子就像曲棍球的橡皮圆盘
If you imagine the hockey puck is a photon.

258
00:16:05,910 --> 00:16:08,190
这里是易北河
This is the river elbe,

259
00:16:08,210 --> 00:16:10,680
有时河面会结冰
and sometimes it freezes over.

260
00:16:11,450 --> 00:16:13,170
假设我等到河面结冰
Supposing I would wait for that

261
00:16:13,360 --> 00:16:15,560
然后推着圆盘过去
and go out there with my hockey puck,

262
00:16:15,570 --> 00:16:17,670
我可以轻而易举地把它打到对岸
I could knock it to the bank with no problem.

263
00:16:18,430 --> 00:16:21,870
但是刚发生大爆炸的宇宙充满了障碍
But the universe just after the big bang was full of obstacles.

264
00:16:22,060 --> 00:16:25,730
假设在我的身边
Now suppose that surrounding me

265
00:16:25,740 --> 00:16:28,690
有一群守门员 他们不守球门
were a bunch of goalies not protecting a goal,

266
00:16:28,690 --> 00:16:31,740
却要阻止我把圆盘打出去
but just making sure that my hockey puck didn't pass them.

267
00:16:31,750 --> 00:16:34,030
所以这些守门员围成一圈
So all these goalies are standing around,

268
00:16:34,040 --> 00:16:36,890
圆盘一打出去 就被他们挡住
and every time I hit the puck, one of them stops it.

269
00:16:37,090 --> 00:16:38,610
不管怎样都穿不过去
This puck is not gonna get through.

270
00:16:39,380 --> 00:16:42,860
赖瑞说 这就是早期的宇宙
This, Larry says, is the early universe.

271
00:16:42,860 --> 00:16:47,290
光子就像圆盘无法通过电子跟质子的守门员
Photon pucks couldn't get past the electron and proton goalies,

272
00:16:47,290 --> 00:16:49,760
所以光无法流动
so light didn't flow.

273
00:16:50,530 --> 00:16:53,570
另一方面 这些守门员也有点特别
On the other hand, these goalies are a little bit unusual,

274
00:16:53,580 --> 00:16:55,590
他们是以一男一女地顺序排列
and they alternate boy, girl, boy, girl,

275
00:16:55,590 --> 00:16:58,560
但他们一开始并不知道因为大家都戴着大面具
but at first, they didn't know that because of their big masks.

276
00:16:58,740 --> 00:17:01,520
不久 一个女生拿下面具
After a while, one of them removes the mask,

277
00:17:01,530 --> 00:17:04,200
旁边的男生就被吸引过去
and the guy next to her says, "oh."

278
00:17:04,590 --> 00:17:06,680
结果圆盘就可以打出去了
Hmm. Then the puck can get right through.

279
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:09,160
一旦光子可以轻易逃脱
Once the photons could escape easily,

280
00:17:09,360 --> 00:17:12,460
世界就出现了重大变化
the world changed dramatically.

281
00:17:15,470 --> 00:17:18,900
在早期的宇宙,光子无法自由移动
In the early universe, photons could never move freely,

282
00:17:18,910 --> 00:17:21,200
因此不可能测得到变化
and there was no way to measure change.

283
00:17:22,150 --> 00:17:26,570
赖瑞认为这就代表时间不存在
Larry argues, that means time did not exist.

284
00:17:26,930 --> 00:17:29,540
只有在重组之后
Only after recombination,

285
00:17:29,550 --> 00:17:31,220
宇宙的温度降低，原子开始形成
when the universe cooled and atoms formed,

286
00:17:32,220 --> 00:17:35,070
这时光才能自由移动
did light begin to move around freely.

287
00:17:36,420 --> 00:17:40,810
赖瑞说这就是宇宙之钟开始运行的时刻
That, says Larry, is when the universe's clock began to tick.

288
00:17:41,380 --> 00:17:44,560
在最早的时候 连时间都不存在
The very earliest point, there's never even a time.

289
00:17:44,560 --> 00:17:46,650
到了最后 时间出现了
But eventually, there was something called time,

290
00:17:46,850 --> 00:17:50,460
而时间会记录事物变化的方式
which was keeping track of the way things changed.

291
00:17:52,230 --> 00:17:55,280
这可以解释我们宇宙的时间是怎么生成的
This could explain the birth of time in our universe.

292
00:17:57,770 --> 00:18:01,960
但如果我们的宇宙毁灭了时间会跟着消失吗？
But if our universe ends, will time die with it?

293
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:06,930
这位物理学家认为时间是最根本的事
This physicist thinks time is truly fundamental --

294
00:18:08,400 --> 00:18:10,300
时间永远存在
time is always here.

295
00:18:10,310 --> 00:18:12,210
只有空间才会生灭
It is space that comes and goes.

296
00:18:16,560 --> 00:18:20,750
时间只会前进 从不会后退
Time moves forward, never backward.

297
00:18:21,530 --> 00:18:25,720
物理学家说这是因为能量一直在散逸
Physicists say that is because energy always dissipates.

298
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:30,300
如果你让时间倒流得够久
If you wind time back far enough,

299
00:18:30,880 --> 00:18:34,500
就会看到整个宇宙的能量聚集在一起
you would see the entire energy of the universe coming together.

300
00:18:35,460 --> 00:18:39,470
在大爆炸的时候一切都凝聚在单一的点
At the big bang, everything is focused on a single point.

301
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:43,590
你无法再把时间往回推
You can't wind time back any more than this.

302
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:46,380
真的是这样吗？
Or can you?

303
00:18:49,450 --> 00:18:53,450
肖恩凯洛是加州理工学院的物理学家
Physicist Sean Carroll of the California institute of technology

304
00:18:53,650 --> 00:18:57,080
他花了不少时间研究时间
has spent much of his career contemplating time.

305
00:18:57,850 --> 00:19:00,520
虽然时间的起点是个谜
Though the origin of time is a mystery,

306
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:02,520
但有件事肖恩很确定
Sean is certain of one thing --

307
00:19:02,530 --> 00:19:07,620
在我们的宇宙 时间是有方向的
in our universe, time has a direction,

308
00:19:08,490 --> 00:19:10,960
就像是贯穿一切事物的箭
an arrow that runs through everything.

309
00:19:11,540 --> 00:19:15,160
时间是测量宇宙变化的量度
Time is a measure of change in the universe.

310
00:19:17,270 --> 00:19:18,980
如果世上没有变化
If nothing were changing in the world,

311
00:19:19,180 --> 00:19:21,090
我们就无法得知时间的流动
there'd be no way of knowing that time was passing.

312
00:19:21,190 --> 00:19:23,390
在每一刻 所有事物都会是一样的
Everything would be the same at every single moment.

313
00:19:23,390 --> 00:19:24,730
这样就不会有时钟
There'd be no clocks.

314
00:19:24,730 --> 00:19:27,210
时间就不会有任何意义
Time itself would basically have no meaning.

315
00:19:31,540 --> 00:19:34,970
只要有变化 不管这个变化有多小
As long as something is changing, no matter how small,

316
00:19:34,980 --> 00:19:36,690
时间就会流动
time is flowing.

317
00:19:37,080 --> 00:19:41,490
而我们的宇宙一直在变化
And our universe is in a constant state of change.

318
00:19:41,850 --> 00:19:43,570
在宇宙即将诞生时
At the dawn of the universe,

319
00:19:43,570 --> 00:19:48,560
巨大的能量被压缩成一小点
an enormous amount of energy was compressed into a single point.

320
00:19:49,150 --> 00:19:51,250
接着发生了大爆炸
Then came the big bang.

321
00:19:52,590 --> 00:19:55,260
从此以后 每过一秒
Since then, with every passing second,

322
00:19:55,450 --> 00:19:58,310
这股能量就扩散得愈广
that energy has become more and more spread out.

323
00:19:58,890 --> 00:20:02,900
测量能量分散的量度叫做熵
The measure of that spreading of energy is called entropy.

324
00:20:03,660 --> 00:20:06,720
肖恩认为时间往前进的运动
Sean believes the forward movement of time,

325
00:20:06,910 --> 00:20:08,250
也就是 时间之箭
time's arrow,

326
00:20:08,250 --> 00:20:12,550
其实是低熵渐渐变成高熵的运动
is the steady movement from low entropy to high entropy.

327
00:20:14,020 --> 00:20:17,260
但时间之箭是怎么射出去的？
But what set time's arrow in motion?

328
00:20:17,840 --> 00:20:21,460
我们的疑惑是熵会不断增加
The puzzle that we have is that entropy tends to increase,

329
00:20:21,660 --> 00:20:24,330
但是大爆炸是非常低熵的状态
but our big bang was a condition of very, very low entropy,

330
00:20:24,520 --> 00:20:26,620
为什么会这样？
so how did it get that way?

331
00:20:26,620 --> 00:20:28,340
大爆炸是从哪里来的？
Where could it have come from?

332
00:20:28,530 --> 00:20:33,100
目前的物理学都说熵会持续增加
Everything we know in physics is things increasing in entropy.

333
00:20:33,110 --> 00:20:34,950
如果你回到大爆炸那一刻
So if you go back to the big bang,

334
00:20:34,950 --> 00:20:38,100
它不可能来自更低熵的地方
there was no lower entropy place it could've come from.

335
00:20:39,650 --> 00:20:45,180
肖恩猜想答案就是我们的宇宙其实是另一个宇宙的孩子
Sean suspects the answer is that our universe is the child of another universe.

336
00:20:45,950 --> 00:20:48,230
然而那个宇宙是什么样子？
But what was that universe like?

337
00:20:49,320 --> 00:20:50,840
也许就会这样
Maybe like this...

338
00:20:51,620 --> 00:20:53,710
想像一个达到均衡的宇宙
Imagine a universe that's in equilibrium.

339
00:20:53,910 --> 00:20:56,230
那是非常高熵的状态
It's in a high-entropy state. It's emptied out.

340
00:20:56,430 --> 00:20:58,410
里面空无一物 只是静静待着
It's just sitting there quietly,

341
00:20:58,410 --> 00:21:00,120
就像这缸水一样
much like the water in this tank.

342
00:21:00,320 --> 00:21:02,030
你看不到任何运动
You don't see any motion.

343
00:21:02,800 --> 00:21:05,080
想像在这个宇宙里
Now imagine in this universe

344
00:21:05,090 --> 00:21:06,990
所有的能量都散逸了
where all the energy is dissipated,

345
00:21:07,190 --> 00:21:11,760
突然出现了一块高能量的区域
suddenly an area of dense energy pops into existence,

346
00:21:12,150 --> 00:21:15,010
就像这包发泡锭一样
much like this bag of effervescent tablets.

347
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:19,920
一开始只有微量而密集的泡泡这是低熵
The seltzer starts small and dense and low entropy

348
00:21:19,930 --> 00:21:22,600
就像刚发生大爆炸的宇宙
just like our universe did near the big bang,

349
00:21:22,600 --> 00:21:25,460
接着宇宙扩张 温度下降 银河形成
but then we expanded and cooled, galaxies formed,

350
00:21:25,660 --> 00:21:29,670
时间之箭就从过去射向未来
and the arrow of time progresses from past to future.

351
00:21:29,870 --> 00:21:33,050
同样的道理 气泡会消散 变成高熵
Likewise, the seltzer fizzes and becomes higher entropy

352
00:21:33,060 --> 00:21:35,150
发泡锭会溶在水里
as it mixes with the water around it.

353
00:21:36,240 --> 00:21:38,140
最后就像我们的宇宙一样
And eventually, just like our universe

354
00:21:38,150 --> 00:21:39,480
回到均衡的状态
will come back to equilibrium

355
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:41,580
时间之箭就会停下来
and the arrow of time will cease,

356
00:21:41,590 --> 00:21:45,020
发泡锭溶到水里 达到均衡
the seltzer reaches equilibrium by mixing with the water around it,

357
00:21:45,210 --> 00:21:47,690
我们就回到没有变化的状态
and we're back to a state that doesn't change anymore,

358
00:21:47,890 --> 00:21:49,790
在这个状态，不会有时间之箭
a state without any arrow of time.

359
00:21:51,140 --> 00:21:53,620
然而没有生命，恒星或固形物
But how could a dead universe,

360
00:21:53,620 --> 00:21:56,110
死寂一片的宇宙怎么可能
one with no life, stars, or solid matter,

361
00:21:56,110 --> 00:21:58,590
生出另一个宇宙？
give birth to another universe?

362
00:22:02,140 --> 00:22:04,140
根据量子力学
According to quantum physics,

363
00:22:04,340 --> 00:22:08,540
即使是虚空也会有微小的能量波动
even an empty void will experience tiny fluctuations of energy.

364
00:22:09,110 --> 00:22:12,260
也就是说 每过一段时间
This means that every once in a while,

365
00:22:13,350 --> 00:22:15,830
就会有东西从虚空中诞生
something can pop out of nothing.

366
00:22:16,980 --> 00:22:20,890
想想放射性元素的原子核
Think about the atomic nucleus of a radioactive element.

367
00:22:20,990 --> 00:22:21,560
它就在那里
It just sits there.

368
00:22:21,760 --> 00:22:24,430
你看不出它有什么变化
You look at it. It's not changing as you look at it,

369
00:22:24,620 --> 00:22:27,860
但是它每一秒都有可能产生衰变
but there is a possibility every second that it will decay,

370
00:22:28,060 --> 00:22:29,960
进而射出新的粒子
that it will spit out a new particle.

371
00:22:30,350 --> 00:22:32,830
我们认为时间和空间
What we're saying is that space-time itself

372
00:22:32,840 --> 00:22:34,930
也可以像原子核一样有放射性
can be radioactive just like that nucleus,

373
00:22:35,030 --> 00:22:38,310
然而它射出的不是新粒子
except instead of spitting out a new particle,

374
00:22:38,500 --> 00:22:40,780
而是全新的宇宙
it can spit out an entirely new universe.

375
00:22:44,350 --> 00:22:48,920
新的宇宙也许会不断产生
New universes may constantly be popping into existence.

376
00:22:52,560 --> 00:22:56,180
或许古老的宇宙有个随机的量子波动
A random quantum fluctuation in an ancient universe --

377
00:22:56,190 --> 00:22:59,620
那个宇宙古老到连时间都不复存在
a universe so old, time fell apart --

378
00:23:00,200 --> 00:23:03,550
或许正是由此制造出我们的宇宙
might even have given birth to our universe.

379
00:23:05,300 --> 00:23:07,580
起初这个过程并没有时间之箭
This process of starting with no arrow of time,

380
00:23:07,780 --> 00:23:10,060
然后它制造出新的宇宙射出时间之箭
budding off a new universe, having an arrow,

381
00:23:10,070 --> 00:23:11,970
这支箭只会飞一阵子
and the arrow only lasts for a little while

382
00:23:12,170 --> 00:23:13,890
宇宙会扩张 温度会下降
as that universe expands and cools,

383
00:23:14,080 --> 00:23:16,170
一旦宇宙达到均衡 箭就会停下来
but once it reaches equilibrium, the arrow stops --

384
00:23:16,560 --> 00:23:19,440
这个过程可能发生过很多次
this could happen many, many, many, many times.

385
00:23:19,440 --> 00:23:20,380
这么说好了
Let's put it that way --

386
00:23:20,390 --> 00:23:24,200
也许它发生的次数多得无从计算至少可以肯定相当多
maybe an infinite number of times, but certainly a very, very large number,

387
00:23:24,400 --> 00:23:27,510
所以我们的宇宙可能不是来自最早的宇宙
so it's possible that the universe we came from

388
00:23:27,510 --> 00:23:28,900
也许我们的大爆炸并非一切的起点
was nowhere near the first.

389
00:23:31,360 --> 00:23:35,160
我们的宇宙时间或许还有更早的祖先
Our big bang might not have been the beginning.

390
00:23:36,550 --> 00:23:41,550
等到我们的宇宙消失了
Our cosmos' time could have ancestors that predated it

391
00:23:41,550 --> 00:23:45,380
或许还会有后代
and descendents after this universe is gone.

392
00:23:46,330 --> 00:23:49,190
但时间或许还有更深奥的真理
But there may be an even deeper truth about time,

393
00:23:49,960 --> 00:23:51,860
若要了解这个真理
a truth we will never learn

394
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:57,010
我们就得接受时间不存在的事实
until we accept that it doesn't really exist.

395
00:24:09,500 --> 00:24:11,400
要是没有时间，我们该怎么办？
What would we do without time?

396
00:24:12,550 --> 00:24:15,410
我们要怎么记下生命中的事件？
How could we keep track of the events in our lives

397
00:24:15,600 --> 00:24:19,800
除了日日年年，分分秒秒还有何方式？
without the steady pulse of minutes, days, and years?

398
00:24:20,760 --> 00:24:24,110
然而这些时间或许都不是真的
But it may be that none of that is real.

399
00:24:25,460 --> 00:24:30,990
时间有可能只是幻觉
It may be that time is nothing more than a mirage.

400
00:24:39,250 --> 00:24:43,640
理论物理学家卡洛罗威利是这么认为的
This is the belief held by theoretical physicist Carlo Rovelli.

401
00:24:44,220 --> 00:24:46,310
卡洛在家乡意大利念书时
As a student in his native Italy,

402
00:24:46,510 --> 00:24:48,410
曾经在前线
Carlo was on the barricades,

403
00:24:48,510 --> 00:24:52,170
对抗死灰复燃的法西斯运动
fighting against the resurgent fascist movement.

404
00:24:52,550 --> 00:24:54,060
我在70年代时 还很年轻
I was young in the '70s,

405
00:24:54,260 --> 00:24:57,500
我胸怀大志 想要改变世界
and there was the big dream of changing the world.

406
00:24:58,270 --> 00:24:59,030
我们失败了
We failed.

407
00:24:59,040 --> 00:25:02,650
我们没有改变世界所以我决定研究科学
We didn't change the world. And so I think I moved into science

408
00:25:02,670 --> 00:25:06,340
我想科学也是改变世界的方式
because I thought it was another way of changing the world,

409
00:25:06,430 --> 00:25:08,710
或许走这条路会比较成功
and perhaps I could be more successful there.

410
00:25:09,670 --> 00:25:13,290
卡洛是吕米尼理论物理中心的负责人
Carlo leaves the centre de physique theorique de luminy,

411
00:25:13,490 --> 00:25:16,350
这是位于法国南部的智库
a think tank in the South of France.

412
00:25:16,930 --> 00:25:19,210
他仍然喜欢打破规则
But he's still breaking the rules.

413
00:25:19,600 --> 00:25:22,560
他是热时间理论的大师
As the leading voice of the theory of thermal time,

414
00:25:23,040 --> 00:25:28,490
正在提倡动摇基础物理学假设的理念
he is raising the banner for a paradigm shift in fundamental physics.

415
00:25:28,490 --> 00:25:29,760
简而言之
In a nutshell,

416
00:25:29,760 --> 00:25:34,510
热时间理论认为时间不存在
thermal time proposes that time does not exist --

417
00:25:34,510 --> 00:25:37,750
至少它不存在于基本层面的现实
at least not at the fundamental level of reality.

418
00:25:39,130 --> 00:25:41,020
基本层面的现实没有时间
The idea that there's no time on the fundamental level

419
00:25:41,020 --> 00:25:42,750
这个概念并不复杂
is not so complicated after all.

420
00:25:42,950 --> 00:25:43,710
让我举个例子
Let me give you an example.

421
00:25:44,710 --> 00:25:47,160
想像你要描述时间里的某件事
Imagine that you describe something happening in time,

422
00:25:47,170 --> 00:25:49,270
例如这个表在时间里摆动
like this is oscillating in time.

423
00:25:49,270 --> 00:25:51,240
也就是说 某个移动的东西
What do we mean? We mean that there is something that moves

424
00:25:51,240 --> 00:25:52,890
跟时间是有关连的
with respect to time.

425
00:25:53,090 --> 00:25:54,030
然而时间是什么？
But what is time?

426
00:25:54,230 --> 00:25:56,330
时间是指针的位置
Time is the position of the hand.

427
00:25:56,530 --> 00:25:58,430
所以我们要观察的
So what we are really observing here,

428
00:25:58,440 --> 00:25:59,380
我们要做的
what we're really doing here

429
00:25:59,390 --> 00:26:04,160
是把这个表的摆动跟指针的运动相比
is comparing this movement with the movement of the hands of the clock.

430
00:26:04,350 --> 00:26:07,430
我们用指针来描述时间变化
So we describe how the hand's changing time,

431
00:26:07,540 --> 00:26:12,880
其实我们看到的只是摆动角度跟指针角度相对的变化
but what we really see is just how this angle changes with respect to this angle.

432
00:26:13,070 --> 00:26:16,340
要是没有时间 我们描述这个世界时
So, do without time means just to describe the world

433
00:26:16,350 --> 00:26:20,730
可以用各种变数的相对变化来形容
in terms of the way the various variables change with respect to one another

434
00:26:20,740 --> 00:26:25,500
而不需要用到这个观察不到的时间
without ever having to bringing this unobservable time into the picture.

435
00:26:30,500 --> 00:26:34,510
牛顿引进了变数T代表时间
Isaac Newton introduced the idea of a variable, "t" for "time,"

436
00:26:34,700 --> 00:26:36,800
以描述物体运动的方式
to describe how objects move.

437
00:26:38,140 --> 00:26:40,040
但是量子力学看待时间的方式
But quantum physics treats time

438
00:26:40,240 --> 00:26:42,910
跟牛顿的古典系统不同
differently than Newton's classical system.

439
00:26:42,910 --> 00:26:48,490
事实上 在实体世界最小的单位也就是普朗克尺度里
In fact, at the planck scale, the smallest unit of the physical world,

440
00:26:48,980 --> 00:26:51,830
时间这个变数根本没有用
time variables simply don't work.

441
00:26:52,610 --> 00:26:55,660
卡洛认为要解决这个矛盾
Carlo thinks the only way to resolve this contradiction

442
00:26:55,660 --> 00:26:57,560
就只能回到牛顿之前的时代
is to go back before Newton

443
00:26:57,760 --> 00:27:00,040
摒弃变数T
and get rid of the variable "t."

444
00:27:00,240 --> 00:27:05,520
他不用时间彻底改写了量子理论的方程式
He has completely reformulated quantum theory without the use of time.

445
00:27:06,350 --> 00:27:08,830
然而好戏还在后头
But that's just the beginning.

446
00:27:10,580 --> 00:27:12,860
有趣的是第二个部分
The interesting part is actually the second part

447
00:27:13,060 --> 00:27:17,070
如果我们接受基本层面没有时间的概念
because if we accept the idea that there's no time on the fundamental level,

448
00:27:17,260 --> 00:27:18,780
然而我们还是感觉得到时间
nevertheless we do experience time.

449
00:27:18,980 --> 00:27:21,460
时间会流动，我们生活在时间里
Time passes for us, right? We live in time.

450
00:27:21,650 --> 00:27:25,590
那么这种感觉是从哪里来的？
So where does this time experience come from?

451
00:27:31,250 --> 00:27:34,480
卡洛认为答案就是热
The answer, Carlo thinks, is heat.

452
00:27:35,260 --> 00:27:37,350
如果你给物质加热
When you add heat to matter,

453
00:27:37,360 --> 00:27:40,410
就会造成不可逆的过程
irreversible processes begin to take place,

454
00:27:40,790 --> 00:27:42,890
也就是无法消除的事件
events that can't be undone.

455
00:27:43,570 --> 00:27:46,250
事物开始在时间里变化
Things begin to change in time.

456
00:27:47,390 --> 00:27:52,520
只要时间出现不可逆的过程 就代表有热
So, every time there is some lack of reversibility in time, there's heat.

457
00:27:53,450 --> 00:27:55,730
因此时间跟热密不可分
So time is tied to heat,

458
00:27:55,740 --> 00:27:57,260
我认为最重要的概念
and I think that the key idea

459
00:27:57,460 --> 00:27:59,170
并非时间产生了热
is not that heat comes from time,

460
00:27:59,370 --> 00:28:01,080
而是热产生了时间
but is that time comes from heat.

461
00:28:01,280 --> 00:28:02,520
热属于热力学的领域
And heat is thermodynamics,

462
00:28:02,520 --> 00:28:06,330
而我们知道热力学由统计数字构成
and we have understood that thermodynamic is statistics.

463
00:28:06,530 --> 00:28:09,590
所以时间跟统计数字密不可分
So time is tied to statistics.

464
00:28:10,560 --> 00:28:13,040
我们无法得知大自然的细微枝节
We don't know the fine details of nature.

465
00:28:13,420 --> 00:28:15,520
我们只能了解平均值
We only understand the average.

466
00:28:16,290 --> 00:28:19,160
我们只具备统计所得的知识
We have only a statistical knowledge.

467
00:28:23,500 --> 00:28:25,020
比方说 卡洛有个炉子
Say Carlo has an oven.

468
00:28:25,600 --> 00:28:29,410
若要测量炉里所有的量子交互作用
To measure all the quantum interactions inside the oven,

469
00:28:29,420 --> 00:28:32,500
他得量上数十亿次
he would need to make billions of measurements.

470
00:28:32,960 --> 00:28:34,300
但这是不可能的任务
But no one can do that.

471
00:28:34,680 --> 00:28:36,500
所以他换个表示方式说
So, instead, he says,

472
00:28:37,060 --> 00:28:40,520
这个炉子有华氏450度
aah! "This oven is 450 degrees."

473
00:28:41,170 --> 00:28:46,520
温度是系统内无数粒子能量的平均值
Temperature is an average of the energies in the countless particles in a system.

474
00:28:47,400 --> 00:28:50,030
如果我们放弃描述量子世界
It's what we get when we give up describing

475
00:28:50,030 --> 00:28:51,990
用这个值表示
what's happening in the quantum world, and,

476
00:28:51,990 --> 00:28:53,880
卡洛认为时间也是一样的
Carlo says, so is time.

477
00:28:55,360 --> 00:28:57,640
如果我们看得到世界的所有细节
If we could see all the details of the world,

478
00:28:57,650 --> 00:29:00,120
我们就会看到没有时间的世界
we would see a timeless world in some sense.

479
00:29:00,320 --> 00:29:02,600
我们感觉得到时间，却看不到它
We wouldn't see this thing that we feel as time.

480
00:29:07,590 --> 00:29:08,920
卡洛认为
To Carlo,

481
00:29:09,310 --> 00:29:11,980
时间只是有限资讯的陈述
time is just a statement of limited information.

482
00:29:13,140 --> 00:29:15,810
宇宙的基本层面是没有时间的
The fundamental level of the universe is timeless.

483
00:29:16,770 --> 00:29:18,860
但是在较大层面的现实
But at larger levels of reality,

484
00:29:19,250 --> 00:29:23,560
一旦物质和热的交互作用出现可见的效应
when the interactions of matter and heat begin to have visible effects,

485
00:29:24,460 --> 00:29:26,400
所谓的时间就此诞生
the thing we call "time" is born.

486
00:29:28,520 --> 00:29:30,710
时间之所以开始
Time began when some system,

487
00:29:30,720 --> 00:29:33,520
是因为某系统不再只跟邻近系统互动
instead of interacting just with its neighbor,

488
00:29:33,520 --> 00:29:35,350
而是跟一大堆系统互动而成
interacted with a big set of systems.

489
00:29:35,350 --> 00:29:40,770
时间之所以开始是因为某系统开始只能取得片面资讯
So time began when some system started having partial information,

490
00:29:40,780 --> 00:29:43,460
无法取得周遭环境完整的资讯
not complete information about its surrounding.

491
00:29:43,570 --> 00:29:47,390
我们的无知创造出时间并且让时间增长
Time begin with our ignorance and grows with our ignorance.

492
00:29:48,540 --> 00:29:50,630
这是相当激进的宇宙观
It's a radical view of the universe,

493
00:29:50,830 --> 00:29:54,440
但是卡洛从来不怕挑战现状
but Carlo has never been afraid to challenge the status quo.

494
00:29:55,520 --> 00:29:57,230
卡洛是对的吗？
Is Carlo correct?

495
00:29:58,000 --> 00:30:02,990
时间真的是因为我们无法了解热扩散才出现的？
Is time really just our failure to comprehend the dispersion of heat?

496
00:30:04,230 --> 00:30:07,080
这名女子说 还有一种可能
This woman says there is another possibility.

497
00:30:07,670 --> 00:30:09,570
时间是真实的
Time is real.

498
00:30:09,570 --> 00:30:14,640
但是它会在每秒内重生一兆兆次
But it is born and reborn a trillion, trillion times a second.

499
00:30:21,090 --> 00:30:23,180
我从甲地走到乙地
When I move from place to place,

500
00:30:24,370 --> 00:30:27,980
我会觉得这是一个连续的动作
my senses tell me it happens in one continuous sweep.

501
00:30:28,760 --> 00:30:31,150
但是根据量子力学的说法
But according to quantum mechanics,

502
00:30:31,620 --> 00:30:38,150
所有的运动只是一连串通过空间的微小抖动
any movement... Is actually a series of microscopic jitters through space.

503
00:30:39,170 --> 00:30:40,500
目前还没有人想出
Huh? No one has yet worked out

504
00:30:40,900 --> 00:30:44,330
要怎么把量子力学的理论套在时间上
how to apply the theory of quantum mechanics to time,

505
00:30:44,720 --> 00:30:47,570
但是有些科学家就快想到了
but some scientists are getting very close.

506
00:30:48,530 --> 00:30:50,250
如果他们成功的话
If they succeed,

507
00:30:50,250 --> 00:30:53,790
我们就得接受一种奇怪的新概念
we will have to accept a strange, new idea --

508
00:30:54,950 --> 00:30:57,620
在每一个短暂的刹那间
every minute fraction of a second,

509
00:30:58,390 --> 00:31:03,920
时间都会不断反覆地诞生
time bursts into existence over and over.

510
00:31:08,450 --> 00:31:12,640
菲道克跟我们一样会感觉到时间的流动
Like all of us, fay dowker experiences a flow of time.

511
00:31:13,220 --> 00:31:14,360
她从一个小女孩
She was a girl...

512
00:31:14,940 --> 00:31:16,840
变成大学生
Then a university student...

513
00:31:16,850 --> 00:31:20,660
如今她成了伦敦帝国学院的物理学家
And now she's a physicist at London's imperial college.

514
00:31:22,330 --> 00:31:25,130
我们最基本的体验就是
Nothing is more fundamental to our experiences than that

515
00:31:25,130 --> 00:31:27,100
对于时间的体验
we have those experiences in time.

516
00:31:27,290 --> 00:31:29,010
我们能够察觉时间的经过
We are aware of time passing.

517
00:31:30,160 --> 00:31:31,870
时间似乎是会流动的
Time seems to flow.

518
00:31:32,480 --> 00:31:34,190
要理解我们的人生
We can hardly make sense of our lives

519
00:31:34,380 --> 00:31:36,980
就得根据已经发生
except in the context of some fixed past of events

520
00:31:36,980 --> 00:31:39,910
而且无法改变的过去事件
that have already happened and that can never be changed

521
00:31:40,300 --> 00:31:45,270
有尚未发生并拥有无限可能的未来事件
and some open future of events that are free and haven't happened yet

522
00:31:45,280 --> 00:31:50,340
以及难以捉摸却分开了过去跟未来的现在
and some mysterious and elusive moment of now that appears to separate the two.

523
00:31:54,580 --> 00:31:56,290
这个道理看似显而易见
This idea seems obvious.

524
00:31:56,680 --> 00:31:58,390
但是它却违反了
But, actually, it goes against

525
00:31:58,590 --> 00:32:02,590
解释宇宙原理的最佳科学理论
our best scientific theory of how the universe works.

526
00:32:04,120 --> 00:32:06,720
相对论告诉我们
The theory of relativity tells us

527
00:32:06,730 --> 00:32:09,400
时间和空间牢牢地结合在一起
space and time are inextricably joined.

528
00:32:09,590 --> 00:32:11,490
所有会存在的时间
All time that will exist

529
00:32:11,690 --> 00:32:15,700
早就存在于所谓的“时空”区块
already exists in a block we call "space-time."

530
00:32:16,460 --> 00:32:19,540
我们一辈子从生到死
As we pass from birth to death,

531
00:32:19,740 --> 00:32:22,650
正是窥见了自己在这里的独有路径
we glimpse our own individual trails

532
00:32:22,650 --> 00:32:25,330
只是走过这张冻结的时空地图
through this frozen space-time landscape.

533
00:32:25,570 --> 00:32:29,310
但是菲认为宇宙不是冻结的区块
But fay believes the universe is not a frozen block.

534
00:32:30,390 --> 00:32:36,120
它是时间和空间的量子颗粒逐渐堆出来的产物
It is a growing pile made of quantum grains of space and time.

535
00:32:36,690 --> 00:32:40,500
在我们眼中，时空是平滑而连续的
Space-time seems smooth and continuous to us,

536
00:32:40,700 --> 00:32:42,420
这是因为我们的身体很大
but that's just because we're very large

537
00:32:42,420 --> 00:32:44,900
而我们用大尺度的观点看事情
and we see things at large scales.

538
00:32:45,500 --> 00:32:49,310
想像我们有一个方块
So, if we imagine that a solid cube of something,

539
00:32:49,320 --> 00:32:50,590
比方说
say a sugar cube,

540
00:32:50,590 --> 00:32:54,090
我们用方糖代表一块时空
represents a piece of space-time,

541
00:32:54,090 --> 00:32:56,680
从远处看
then from far away,

542
00:32:56,680 --> 00:32:58,410
方糖是一块固体
that looks solid. It looks like a chunk.

543
00:32:58,500 --> 00:33:00,780
但是如果我们把方糖放大
But we know that if you zoom in on it

544
00:33:00,990 --> 00:33:02,490
再观察它更基本的结构
and look at its more fundamental structure,

545
00:33:02,490 --> 00:33:04,600
就会发现它是由颗粒组成的
we see that it breaks up into grains.

546
00:33:05,000 --> 00:33:08,610
时空是颗粒的模型就依照同样的道理
The idea with a granular model of space-time is similar.

547
00:33:08,810 --> 00:33:13,500
从基本的微小尺度来看它是由颗粒组成的
At fundamental, tiny scales, it's grainy and particulate.

548
00:33:13,500 --> 00:33:15,600
从大尺度来看 它是平滑而连续的
At large scales, it appears smooth and continuous.

549
00:33:15,610 --> 00:33:17,700
看不出有颗粒的性质
We don't notice that granularity.

550
00:33:20,590 --> 00:33:23,440
那么时空的颗粒有多小？
Just how small is a grain of space-time?

551
00:33:24,220 --> 00:33:26,510
小到难以理解
Inconceivably small.

552
00:33:27,480 --> 00:33:31,670
大概是一百万兆兆兆分之一秒
Roughly a million, trillion, trillion, trillionth of a second.

553
00:33:32,250 --> 00:33:38,580
物理学家认为这是最小的量度单位
This is what physicists believe is the smallest possible unit of measurement.

554
00:33:39,350 --> 00:33:41,250
菲认为时空
Fay thinks space-time is built

555
00:33:41,450 --> 00:33:46,420
能由这种细微的颗粒大量聚积而成的
from a prodigious stack of these impossibly tiny grains,

556
00:33:46,610 --> 00:33:49,660
她把这种颗粒称为时空原子
which she calls "space-time atoms."

557
00:33:51,590 --> 00:33:54,450
时空原子结合了两种概念
This marries together two concepts --

558
00:33:54,460 --> 00:33:57,130
第一 时空基本上是原子
that space-time is fundamentally atomic

559
00:33:57,130 --> 00:34:00,560
从极小的尺度来看是一颗颗的
or bitty or granular at very tiny scales

560
00:34:01,560 --> 00:34:04,230
第二则是因果律的概念
with the notion of causality,

561
00:34:04,420 --> 00:34:08,230
也就是说 先有因才有果
the fact that cause must precede effect.

562
00:34:08,240 --> 00:34:11,090
比方说如果我听到巨大的声响
So, for example, if I hear a loud noise...

563
00:34:13,010 --> 00:34:16,440
我会吓一跳或许还会打翻咖啡杯
...then that will startle me, and I might drop my cup of coffee.

564
00:34:17,400 --> 00:34:19,500
这里的因就是声响
So the cause was the loud noise.

565
00:34:19,690 --> 00:34:22,170
果就是打翻咖啡杯
The effect was the dropping of my cup of coffee.

566
00:34:27,560 --> 00:34:30,040
根据相对论坚持的说法
If, as relativity insists,

567
00:34:30,420 --> 00:34:34,230
所有的时空早就存在了
all of space and time already exist,

568
00:34:34,810 --> 00:34:40,640
不管你从过去 现在或未来的角度看咖啡杯都会被打翻
the coffee cup will always fall, is always falling, has always fallen.

569
00:34:41,510 --> 00:34:43,230
但是在菲的眼中
But in fay's view,

570
00:34:43,420 --> 00:34:46,860
宇宙是一组事件的集合这些事件会不断增加
the universe is a set of events that is forever growing.

571
00:34:48,010 --> 00:34:53,350
她把这些相连的事件顺序称为因果组我们在观察因果组时
When we observe these connected sequences of events, what she calls a causal set,

572
00:34:53,350 --> 00:34:56,510
会感觉到时间的流动
we perceive that time is passing.

573
00:34:58,170 --> 00:35:03,700
因果组会因为新的时空原子累积而增长
A causal set can grow by the accumulation of new space-time atoms.

574
00:35:04,090 --> 00:35:07,710
这些新的时空原子的生成
And this birth of new space-time atoms

575
00:35:07,910 --> 00:35:12,410
可能就是我们所知的时间流动
could be the passage of time as we know it.

576
00:35:13,480 --> 00:35:15,960
我们体验到的现在
What we experience as the present

577
00:35:16,160 --> 00:35:19,210
就是这种新的时空原子的生成
is the birth of these new space-time atoms.

578
00:35:19,400 --> 00:35:21,880
旧的原子并未消失
The old atoms don't die.

579
00:35:21,880 --> 00:35:25,120
它只是堆积在所谓的过去里
They pile up into the thing we call "the past."

580
00:35:25,700 --> 00:35:27,980
未来尚未生成
The future has yet to be born.

581
00:35:29,070 --> 00:35:33,180
一旦时空原子生成并且存在
Once a space-time atom is born and exists,

582
00:35:33,580 --> 00:35:36,050
它就会形成过去一部分
it will then form part of the past.

583
00:35:36,060 --> 00:35:40,450
因此我们才会觉得过去是固定的
So, in that sense, it also realizes our sense that the past is fixed,

584
00:35:40,450 --> 00:35:43,310
是已经发生 不可改变的
that the past has happened, and that it cannot be changed.

585
00:35:47,520 --> 00:35:50,580
时间或许不是连续的河流
Time may not be a continuous river,

586
00:35:50,580 --> 00:35:52,860
而是无止尽的事件集合
but rather an endless rain of events.

587
00:35:54,030 --> 00:35:56,700
哪一种时间概念才是正确的？
So, which concept of time is correct?

588
00:35:57,660 --> 00:36:00,140
我们是否有更接近时间的起点？
Are we getting closer to the origin of time?

589
00:36:01,100 --> 00:36:02,430
也许我们很快就会知道
We may soon know.

590
00:36:03,590 --> 00:36:05,110
在这间实验室
In this laboratory,

591
00:36:05,310 --> 00:36:08,540
研究人员正在设计新的实验
researchers are working on a new experiment

592
00:36:08,740 --> 00:36:13,350
它或许会彻底改变我们对于时间和宇宙的认识
that could forever change our understanding of time and the universe.

593
00:36:18,540 --> 00:36:21,520
或许时间源自大爆炸
Time may have begun at the big bang.

594
00:36:23,570 --> 00:36:26,050
或许它一直在流动着
It may have always been flowing.

595
00:36:26,630 --> 00:36:31,010
或许它在每秒间会生成好几兆次
Or it could be born trillions of times every second.

596
00:36:32,550 --> 00:36:36,210
这个辩论可能会再持续几十年
This debate could go on for decades.

597
00:36:36,210 --> 00:36:38,490
也可能会马上结束
Or it could end any day now.

598
00:36:39,060 --> 00:36:42,130
因为我们终于有可能用实验
Because we may finally have an experiment

599
00:36:42,130 --> 00:36:45,560
揭开时间的真面目
that reveals the true nature of time.

600
00:36:49,580 --> 00:36:53,020
在加州大学柏克莱分校
At the Berkeley campus of the university of California,

601
00:36:53,020 --> 00:36:56,640
哈慕海夫纳教授正在制造时间环
Professor Hartmut haeffner is building a time ring --

602
00:36:58,400 --> 00:37:01,260
它会像这个金属环一样旋转
an object that will rotate like this disk.

603
00:37:02,790 --> 00:37:07,560
这个金属环是用电磁力漂在空中
But while this metal ring is levitated using electromagnetic force,

604
00:37:08,140 --> 00:37:11,570
但时间环的动力是来自时间的跳动
a time ring will be driven by a jitter in time.

605
00:37:13,680 --> 00:37:15,660
如果这项实验能够成功
If it works,

606
00:37:15,660 --> 00:37:18,250
就能证明颇受争议的理论
this experiment will prove a controversial theory --

607
00:37:19,340 --> 00:37:22,960
在空间里观察到的量子波动
the quantum fluctuations that have been observed in space

608
00:37:23,160 --> 00:37:25,560
也存在于时间里
also exist in time.

609
00:37:26,510 --> 00:37:28,410
我们物理学家喜欢对称
We physicists like symmetries,

610
00:37:28,420 --> 00:37:31,950
其中一种对称就是时间与空间
and one symmetry is like space and time.

611
00:37:32,550 --> 00:37:34,830
我们想把它们平等看待
We would like to treat them on the same footing,

612
00:37:34,840 --> 00:37:37,510
我们在空间里观察到的现象
so whatever we observe in space,

613
00:37:37,710 --> 00:37:40,180
应该也会出现在时间里
we think we should also see in time,

614
00:37:40,190 --> 00:37:43,480
这样对于宇宙的描述就变得更简单，
and this would actually simplify the description of the universe

615
00:37:43,480 --> 00:37:45,560
更优美
or make it more elegant.

616
00:37:46,020 --> 00:37:49,550
同在柏克莱做研究的奈米科学家李彤昌
Nanotechnologist Tongcang Li, also at Berkeley,

617
00:37:50,260 --> 00:37:53,300
设计了这个时间环实验
devised the time-ring experiment.

618
00:37:53,300 --> 00:37:54,820
他找上哈慕
He approached Hartmut,

619
00:37:54,830 --> 00:37:58,060
因为哈慕是捕捉与研究原子粒子的专家
an expert in trapping and studying atomic particles.

620
00:37:58,840 --> 00:38:00,360
但是哈慕心存疑虑
But Hartmut had his doubts.

621
00:38:01,440 --> 00:38:03,150
一开始我觉得
In the beginning, I mean, I was thinking,

622
00:38:03,160 --> 00:38:05,440
这个想法太疯狂
"I mean, they are crazy.

623
00:38:05,440 --> 00:38:06,590
太荒谬了
I mean, this is a ridiculous idea,"

624
00:38:06,590 --> 00:38:07,730
结果我们谈过以后
and then we start to talking,

625
00:38:07,740 --> 00:38:11,550
我才发现这个想法虽然很怪
and I realized, "oh, wait. "This is really weird,

626
00:38:11,750 --> 00:38:13,940
但它是对的，应该要这样才对
but they are right. This is the way it should be."

627
00:38:16,570 --> 00:38:20,570
这个电极的内部跟一根人类毛发一样宽
On this electrode, inside a space the width of a human hair,

628
00:38:21,150 --> 00:38:25,720
哈慕的团队会用它制造出完美的静态空间
Hartmut and his team will create a perfectly static landscape --

629
00:38:25,730 --> 00:38:29,180
这个空间会跟外界的能量隔离
a landscape isolated from outside energy.

630
00:38:30,540 --> 00:38:32,630
为了进一步降低电极里的能量
To further reduce energy in the system,

631
00:38:32,640 --> 00:38:36,070
他必顶捕捉并冷却钙离子
he must trap and cool calcium ions

632
00:38:36,080 --> 00:38:40,460
冷却到只比绝对零度高几十亿分之一度
down to a few billionths of a degree above absolute zero --

633
00:38:40,660 --> 00:38:44,570
这是史上冷却到最低的温度
colder than anything has ever been cooled before.

634
00:38:46,410 --> 00:38:50,030
这会让钙离子回到基态
This will take the ions down to their ground state --

635
00:38:50,040 --> 00:38:52,520
也就是最小能量的状态
the state of minimum possible energy.

636
00:38:53,100 --> 00:38:57,860
只有这样才能把时间跟空间的效应隔开
Only then can the effects of space be separated from time.

637
00:38:58,250 --> 00:39:01,510
想像这些滚珠是钙离子
Imagine these ball bearings are calcium ions

638
00:39:01,610 --> 00:39:06,570
我们会把一百个钙离子注入真空室
and we're going to inject 100 of these calcium ions into our vacuum chamber.

639
00:39:06,760 --> 00:39:08,100
在常温下
So, at normal temperatures,

640
00:39:08,300 --> 00:39:12,330
这些离子会往随机的方向快速移动
these ions move around rapidly in random directions,

641
00:39:12,520 --> 00:39:15,750
但如果温度降低离子就会形成这个环 还会变慢
but when we cool them, they form this ring and they slow down,

642
00:39:15,760 --> 00:39:20,480
按理说这个环早晚会停止移动
and you would expect that at some point, this ring stops moving.

643
00:39:20,580 --> 00:39:22,390
不会旋转
It wouldn't rotate,

644
00:39:22,580 --> 00:39:24,860
但是如果这个理论没错
but if this theory is correct,

645
00:39:24,870 --> 00:39:28,110
这个环应该会开始转动
that ring should move, rotate, spin.

646
00:39:31,570 --> 00:39:34,430
处于基态的物体不应该会动
An object at ground state shouldn't move,

647
00:39:34,440 --> 00:39:38,050
因为它没有消耗或产生能量
because it neither consumes nor produces energy.

648
00:39:39,210 --> 00:39:41,110
但是量子力学告诉我们
But quantum mechanics tells us

649
00:39:41,120 --> 00:39:44,930
零不等于零
zero does not mean zero.

650
00:39:44,940 --> 00:39:49,250
就算在基态 还是会有量子波动
Even at ground state, there will still be quantum fluctuations.

651
00:39:49,530 --> 00:39:53,160
在量子力学向来会有这种有限的跳动
In quantum mechanics, there's always this finite jitter motion

652
00:39:53,360 --> 00:39:55,640
在基态的物体还是会移动
in the ground state. Things will still move,

653
00:39:55,840 --> 00:39:58,540
但是它的运动是不定向的
but they will move in an undirected way.

654
00:39:58,640 --> 00:40:01,120
而我们要找的现象...
What we are after is something

655
00:40:01,310 --> 00:40:04,550
是有特定方向的运动
where there is still motion in a particular direction.

656
00:40:04,560 --> 00:40:07,800
差异之处在于这是有方向性的
It would be different in the sense that it's directed.

657
00:40:11,530 --> 00:40:16,680
冷冻的离子只能在空间里产生微小而随机的运动
Freezing the ions will allow them to make only tiny, random movements in space --

658
00:40:17,490 --> 00:40:20,160
小到无法让这个环移动
too small to make the ring move.

659
00:40:20,540 --> 00:40:23,980
但如果离子环还是开始转动
But if the ion ring begins to turn anyway,

660
00:40:24,740 --> 00:40:28,550
那就表示时间有波动
it will mean there has been a fluctuation in time.

661
00:40:28,940 --> 00:40:30,580
从理论的角度来看
From the theory perspective,

662
00:40:30,580 --> 00:40:35,270
目前还不清楚如此低温会造成什么结果
it's not at all clear what is going to happen at these low temperatures.

663
00:40:35,570 --> 00:40:38,430
有人说这个环会移动
There are people who say that this ring should move,

664
00:40:38,630 --> 00:40:40,340
有人说不会
and others say it shouldn't.

665
00:40:41,590 --> 00:40:43,750
如果时间环实验成功了
If the time ring works,

666
00:40:43,750 --> 00:40:46,560
那么空间和时间都有波动
then both space and time fluctuate.

667
00:40:47,320 --> 00:40:49,520
或许这可以支持菲道克的理论
That might support fay dowker's theory

668
00:40:49,530 --> 00:40:53,340
在量子的层面所见时空是会持续生成累积的
that space-time is constantly generating itself in quantum dips.

669
00:40:55,450 --> 00:40:58,220
至少这项实验可以显示
At the very least, it will demonstrate

670
00:40:58,230 --> 00:41:02,420
在量子领域时空确实是密不可分的
that space and time are inextricably linked in the quantum realm.

671
00:41:03,990 --> 00:41:07,050
空间有量子波动
So, we have these quantum fluctuations in space,

672
00:41:07,620 --> 00:41:11,430
但是我们把时间视为非常精确的东西
but time we treat as something which you can know very precisely.

673
00:41:11,440 --> 00:41:15,060
其实我更想知道
Well, actually, what I would be feeling much more happy with

674
00:41:15,260 --> 00:41:18,500
量子力学是否也能证明时间是模糊的
is if quantum mechanics would also assume that time is fuzzy,

675
00:41:18,700 --> 00:41:20,160
也就是说
so to speak,

676
00:41:20,160 --> 00:41:23,480
你无法知道确切的时间
that you can't tell what time it is exactly,

677
00:41:23,490 --> 00:41:27,300
只能知道大概 因为时间有波动
only approximately, that you have fluctuations of time.

678
00:41:27,500 --> 00:41:29,990
我从来没看过时间波动
And I've never worked with something where time fluctuates,

679
00:41:29,990 --> 00:41:30,950
所以...
so...

680
00:41:31,910 --> 00:41:33,050
也许等我看到了
When I see it,

681
00:41:33,050 --> 00:41:35,150
就会觉得这是理所当然的
maybe then it becomes natural to me, too.

682
00:41:40,530 --> 00:41:44,340
如果我们找到时间的起点
If we find the origins of time,

683
00:41:44,350 --> 00:41:47,600
就能解开宇宙最深奥的谜题之一
we will answer one of the deepest riddles of creation.

684
00:41:49,440 --> 00:41:51,720
但是我们也会发现
But we might also learn

685
00:41:51,920 --> 00:41:54,200
对宇宙而言 时间毫无意义
that time is meaningless to the universe --

686
00:41:55,360 --> 00:41:57,260
时间只对我们有意义
time only matters to us

687
00:41:58,030 --> 00:41:59,580
因为它让我们不会迷失
because it anchors us

688
00:41:59,580 --> 00:42:02,520
在过去的回忆
between our memories of the past...

689
00:42:03,520 --> 00:42:07,590
与未来的谜团里
And the mystery of the future.

